15 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Oncoprint-style heatmap showing principal variants in antifungal resistance candidate genes among 82 Candidozyma auris isolates from the Russian Federation. Rows correspond to selected genes from the 74-gene antifungal resistance candidate panel, and columns correspond to individual isolates. Colors indicate the predicted consequence of each variant. The figure provides a visual overview of the distribution of major resistance-associated variants across the isolate collection.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Bayesian phylogenetic tree of 82 Russian Candidozyma auris isolates inferred under the GTR substitution model in BEAST. The tree is shown in a circular layout, with isolate labels arranged around the perimeter. Posterior probabilities are displayed at internal nodes. Tip colors indicate the region of isolation: Saint Petersburg, Leningrad oblast, Moscow, and Moscow oblast. The figure illustrates phylogenetic relationships and geographic structuring among Russian C. auris isolates.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Two box plots showing genomic diversity of Candidozyma auris isolates from Russia. Panel a shows the distribution of per-isolate mean pairwise SNP distances for isolates from Moscow and St. Petersburg. Panel b shows raw pairwise SNP distances for isolate pairs from the same hospital and from different hospitals. Individual observations are overlaid as points, and boxplots show the median, interquartile range, and whiskers. Mann\205Whitney U test p-values and effect sizes are shown above the plots.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Time-calibrated phylogeny of 82 Russian Candidozyma auris isolates. The tree was inferred in IQ-TREE using tip dates corresponding to isolate collection dates. Internal node labels indicate inferred dates of the most recent common ancestors. Tip colors indicate the region of isolation: Saint Petersburg, Leningrad oblast, Moscow, and Moscow oblast. Colored squares denote the originating healthcare institution. The figure visualizes temporal, geographic, and hospital-associated structure within the Russian C. auris isolate collection.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
